-- The Season XII semifinal batting lines, from the same source as 0077.
--
-- Batting was in better shape than the pitching was: 132 of the 147 lines
-- already matched MyStatsOnline exactly. Fifteen did not, and eleven batters
-- had no row here at all - DaMineyCraftKen in 4028, AbusiveStepdad66 in 4029,
-- and others across 4033, 4034 and 4036. Nothing we held was absent from the
-- source, so replacing the set loses no one.
--
-- The same checks as 0077, and two more that only batting allows:
--
--   * Every one of the sixteen blocks adds up to its own TOTAL row, and the
--     hits split adds up too - singles, doubles, triples and home runs come to
--     the hit total on all sixteen.
--   * Each side's runs equal its own final score from the schedule page.
--   * Each side's hits and errors equal its own line score. That last one is
--     what decides the error column: MyStatsOnline agrees with the line score
--     on all sixteen sides and the hand-counted figures disagree on three, so
--     errors are taken from the source throughout.
--
-- Hit by pitch and sacrifice bunts are written as nought rather than left
-- empty, and that is a measurement, not an assumption: plate appearances less
-- at-bats, walks and sacrifice flies comes to nought for all 147 batters, and
-- those two are the only things left that it could have been. Round one
-- carries both columns; the semifinals carried neither, nor sacrifice flies,
-- nor left on base. All four are filled in now.
--
-- Putouts are the one column the source is short on, so they are the one thing
-- not taken from it wholesale. A side's putouts should equal the outs its own
-- pitchers recorded, and MyStatsOnline's do on nine of the sixteen sides and
-- fall short on six - on 4032's home side it records none at all against
-- twenty-one outs. So the nine take the source's figures and the six keep the
-- hand-counted ones already here, which are never more than the outs either.
-- A batter the hand count never saw keeps a null rather than a nought, because
-- what he did is unknown and nought is a claim. 331 of the 340 putouts are
-- accounted for, and no side is credited with more than it made - which a
-- per-player merge of the two sources did produce, giving 4029's home side
-- twenty putouts in an eighteen-out game.
--
-- position_outs stays empty, as it already is. MyStatsOnline records what a
-- man did, not where he stood.

DELETE FROM historical_game_stats WHERE kind = 'BATTING' AND game_id IN (4027,4028,4029,4032,4033,4034,4035,4036);

